            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "There's also little point in having to update every single repository when cli11 has a new version... the vast majority of our subproject wrap files use HEAD so that we don't have to mess with them ever.\n\nCan we revert this back?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "wrapfiles also do not affect unit testing.  Unit tests all use the specified version from openbmc-build-scripts.  This only affects developers that chose to use wrap file builds."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "> Can we revert this back?\n\nI would prefer not to."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "> wrapfiles also do not affect unit testing. Unit tests all use the specified version from openbmc-build-scripts.\n\nRight, I was/am aware of how this works.  By \"unit testing\" I meant my own personal invoking of the tests using the wraps."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Have you seen cases where this has actually been a problem for you?  Can you please point to commits that happened in CLI11 that broke your development?\n\nWe have seen many cases where repositories use some specific version in their wrap file and the maintainer doesn't update it for 3 years.  This is what I don't want to see."
                }
            ],
